# MathBridge Core Standards

- Build for accessibility-first UX and semantics by default.
- Prefer TypeScript with explicit types at API boundaries.
- Keep server secrets on the server only; never expose API keys in client code.
- Use `process.env` for credentials and provide `.env.example` placeholders only.
- Keep changes small, testable, and aligned to the active PRD tasks.

## Security Rules

- Never hardcode secrets or tokens in source, docs, or examples.
- Validate and sanitize all untrusted input before processing.
- Return user-safe errors from APIs; do not leak stack traces or provider internals.

## Delivery Rules

- Add concise docs updates when behavior or setup changes.
- Favor simple architecture first, then add complexity only when required.
